<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila promises access to its rice market by 2005.</title>
<headline>Manila promises access to its rice market by 2005.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines is committed to liberalise rice importation from neigbouring countries by the year 2005, Agriculture Secretary Salvador Escudero said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Rice will definitely be phased-in ...in the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement-Common Effective Preferential Tariff,&quot; Escudero told reporters.</p>
<p>Under the plan, quantitative restrictions on rice imports from members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) will be removed and its tariff gradually reduced.</p>
<p>ASEAN includes the Philippines, Thailand, Singapore, Brunei, Malaysia, Vietnam and Indonesia.</p>
<p>The Philippines restricts rice importation at present to protect local farmers from an influx of cheaper rice from other countries.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
